\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\kerning0\b LangGraph\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}LangGraph\b0  is a framework built on top of LangChain specifically designed for developing \b stateful, agent-based applications\b0 . While LangChain excels at creating linear workflows and chains, LangGraph enables developers to build complex workflows involving multiple agents, conditional logic, loops, branching, and persistent state.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}LangGraph treats an AI application as a \b graph\b0 , where each node represents an action, agent, or computation, and edges define how information flows between these nodes.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}It is particularly useful for building advanced Agentic AI systems where tasks require planning, reasoning, collaboration between multiple agents, and iterative decision-making.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\kerning2\b Why LangGraph?\par
\b0 Traditional LangChain chains follow a sequential approach:\par
Plain Text\par
Input \f1\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Step 1 \f1\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Step 2 \f1\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Step 3 \f1\u8594?\f0\lang16393  Output\par
However, real-world AI systems often require:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Multiple agents working together\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Decision branches\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Task retries\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Iterative reasoning\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Human-in-the-loop approval\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Long-running workflows\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 LangGraph solves these challenges by introducing graph-based orchestration.\par
