\b Multi-Agent Coordination Patterns (MCP)\par
Multi-Agent Coordination Patterns (MCP)\b0  are architectural patterns that define how multiple AI agents communicate, collaborate, delegate tasks, share information, and coordinate decision-making to achieve a common objective. Rather than relying on a single agent to handle an entire workflow, MCP divides responsibilities among specialized agents, improving scalability, reliability, and problem-solving capabilities.\par
In modern Agentic AI systems, each agent is typically designed with a specific role, expertise, or responsibility. Coordination patterns determine how these agents interact, exchange context, resolve dependencies, and collectively reach goals. Frameworks such as \b LangGraph\b0 , \b CrewAI\b0 , \b AutoGen\b0 , and \b Semantic Kernel\b0  commonly implement these patterns.\par
\par
\b Why Multi-Agent Coordination?\par
\b0 As tasks become more complex, a single agent may struggle with:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Large reasoning chains\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Domain-specific specialization\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Parallel execution requirements\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Error handling\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Scalability concerns\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Multi-agent systems overcome these limitations by distributing work among specialized agents.\par
For example, in a Financial Leakage Detection System:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Data Collection Agent gathers transactions.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Anomaly Detection Agent identifies suspicious activity.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Risk Assessment Agent evaluates severity.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Report Generation Agent creates investigation summaries.\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Notification Agent alerts stakeholders.\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Each agent contributes expertise while working toward a common objective.\par
\par
\b 1. Supervisor-Worker Pattern\par
\b0 This is one of the most common coordination models.\par
A central \b Supervisor Agent\b0  manages multiple Worker Agents and orchestrates task execution.\par
\b Responsibilities\par
\b0 Supervisor:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Receives objective\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Breaks work into subtasks\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Assigns tasks\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Collects results\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Produces final output\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Workers:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Execute assigned tasks\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Return results\par

\pard\widctlpar\sa160\sl276\slmult1\b Example\par
\b0 Software Development Assistant:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sa160\sl276\slmult1 Supervisor Agent receives feature request\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Developer Agent writes code\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Testing Agent validates code\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Reviewer Agent performs quality checks\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Supervisor combines outputs\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\kerning36\b 2. Sequential Pipeline Pattern\par
\kerning0\b0 Agents work in a predefined sequence, with each agent consuming the previous agent's output.\par
\b Use Cases\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\b0 RAG Pipelines\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Document analysis\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}Data processing workflows\par
{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}ETL operations\par

\pard\widctlpar\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0\par
\b 3. Collaborative Peer-to-Peer Pattern\par
\b0 Here, agents interact directly with one another without a central controller.\par
Agents negotiate, share findings, and jointly solve problems.\par
\b Example\par
\b0 Research Assistant System:\par

\pard{\pntext\f3\'B7\tab}{\*\pn\pnlvlblt\pnf3\pnindent360{\pntxtb\'B7}}\widctlpar\fi-360\li720\sb100\sa100\sl300\slmult0 Market Research Agent\par
